---
import SiteNav from "../components/SiteNav.astro";
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Personal showcase for Bryant Hayden: educator, STEM mentor, builder, and systems thinker."
    />
    <title>Bryant Hayden — SCADA / MES Developer</title>
    <meta property="og:title" content="Bryant Hayden — SCADA / MES Developer" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Industrial automation, SCADA, MES, and production systems portfolio." />
    <meta property="og:image" content="/og-preview.svg" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="/og-preview.svg" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body class="about-page">
    <SiteNav active="personal" />

    <main>
      <section class="about-hero">
        <div class="container about-hero__grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Personal Showcase</p>
            <h1>A builder, teacher, and systems thinker.</h1>
            <p class="lead">
              My career has moved through education, hands-on STEM, computer science, and industrial software. The common
              thread is helping people understand complex systems and turning that understanding into something useful.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="about-portrait">
            <img src="/images/headshot.jpg" alt="Headshot of Bryant Hayden" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section about-story">
        <div class="container about-story__grid">
          <article class="about-story__intro">
            <p class="eyebrow">The throughline</p>
              <h2 class="section__title">The person behind the technical work.</h2>
          </article>
          <div class="about-story__body">
            <p>
              Before working in industrial software, I taught music and worked with students through robotics, LEGO, and
              Rubik's Cube activities. Teaching shaped how I approach technical work: listen first, explain clearly, and build
              something that the person using it can actually trust.
            </p>
            <p>
              Computer science gave me the formal foundation to design software, work with data, and reason about systems. In
              manufacturing, that foundation became practical: applications have to work during production, communicate with
              equipment, and remain supportable after they are commissioned.
            </p>
            <p>
              Those experiences shaped the way I approach every challenge: stay curious, communicate clearly, and make the
              result useful to the people who depend on it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section about-pillars">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section__header">
            <p class="eyebrow">Outside the job title</p>
            <h2 class="section__title">The experiences that shaped me</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="grid about-pillars__grid">
            <article class="card about-pillar">
              <span class="about-pillar__number">01</span>
              <h3>Teaching &amp; communication</h3>
              <p>
                Music education and STEM clubs taught me to meet people where they are, make difficult ideas approachable,
                and help others become confident with unfamiliar tools.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="card about-pillar">
              <span class="about-pillar__number">02</span>
              <h3>Academic &amp; independent work</h3>
              <p>
                A B.S. in Computer Science and projects such as an autonomous Rubik's Cube robot and a full-stack Wordle game
                gave me a broad software and problem-solving foundation.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="card about-pillar">
              <span class="about-pillar__number">03</span>
              <h3>Curiosity and making</h3>
              <p>
                I enjoy taking ideas apart, understanding how they work, and building practical versions that others can use
                and learn from.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section personal-project">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section__header">
            <p class="eyebrow">Personal project / Making</p>
            <h2 class="section__title">Stirling engine build</h2>
          </div>
          <article class="project-hero personal-project__hero">
            <div class="project-hero__media">
              <figure class="project-video">
                <iframe
                  src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/HJgJ5IBwwfw"
                  title="Bryant Hayden Stirling engine build"
                  loading="lazy"
                  allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
                  allowfullscreen
                ></iframe>
                <figcaption>Hands-on engine build</figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>
            <div class="project-hero__content">
              <p class="project-tag">Personal / Fabrication</p>
              <h3>Making a mechanical system understandable.</h3>
              <p>
                This Stirling engine project shows the hands-on side of how I learn: understand the physical system, work
                through constraints, and turn a complex mechanism into something observable and useful.
              </p>
              <div class="project-hero__tags" aria-label="Stirling engine project themes">
                <span>Mechanical systems</span>
                <span>Fabrication</span>
                <span>Problem solving</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section personal-project personal-project--robot">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section__header">
            <p class="eyebrow">Personal project / Robotics</p>
            <h2 class="section__title">Autonomous Rubik's Cube solving bot</h2>
          </div>
          <article class="project-hero personal-project__hero">
            <div class="project-hero__media">
              <figure class="project-video">
                <iframe
                  src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/_tdodO76_XQ"
                  title="Bryant Hayden autonomous Rubik's Cube solving robot"
                  loading="lazy"
                  allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
                  allowfullscreen
                ></iframe>
                <figcaption>Robot solving demonstration</figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>
            <div class="project-hero__content">
              <p class="project-tag">Personal / Robotics</p>
              <h3>From computer vision to physical motion.</h3>
              <p>
                An autonomous Rubik's Cube robot that brings together software, computer vision, actuators, CAD, and
                hands-on fabrication. It reflects the same systems mindset I bring to production work: observe, decide, and
                execute against the physical world.
              </p>
              <div class="project-hero__tags" aria-label="Rubik's Cube robot project themes">
                <span>Python</span>
                <span>Computer vision</span>
                <span>Raspberry Pi</span>
                <span>CAD / 3D printing</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section about-values">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="card about-values__card">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">How I work</p>
              <h2 class="section__title">Practical, curious, and accountable.</h2>
            </div>
            <ul class="skill-list">
              <li>Start with the people and process, not just the technology</li>
              <li>Test changes deliberately before they reach production</li>
              <li>Document systems so others can support and extend them</li>
              <li>Teach the solution until the team can use it with confidence</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section about-next">
        <div class="container about-next__content">
            <p class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</p>
            <h2 class="section__title">See the professional work behind the story.</h2>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="button button--primary" href="/journey">Professional Showcase</a>
            <a class="button button--secondary" href="/resume">Read My Resume</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div class="container footer__content">
        <p>© 2026 Bryant Hayden</p>
        <p>IT/OT • SCADA • MES • IIoT</p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
